{
  "$comment": [
    "THE gate registry. This file is the single answer to 'what must pass?'.",
    "",
    "Before it existed there were three divergent answers: init.sh ran 62 contract",
    "checks, .github/workflows/ci.yml ran 32, and tools/run_ci_locally.sh \u2014 the",
    "self-described 'mirror' of ci.yml \u2014 ran 25. An agent could not determine what",
    "'correct' meant, and 21 checks were enforced nowhere but a bootstrap script.",
    "",
    "Every runner now reads this file: tools/verify_contracts.sh executes it,",
    "init.sh calls --scope env, run_ci_locally.sh and ci.yml call --scope ci.",
    "tools/gates_registry_check.py fails CI if any tools/*_check.py is neither",
    "registered here nor listed in `excluded`, so coverage cannot silently rot.",
    "",
    "Per-scope args matter: 22 checks take --require-cargo, which turns 'cargo not on",
    "PATH -> skipped, still passes' into a hard failure (see backtest_check.py:344).",
    "init.sh passed it; ci.yml did not. Dropping it would have silently weakened 22",
    "gates, so scopes carry their own argv."
  ],
  "scopes": {
    "env": "init.sh at bootstrap. The structural subset that proves a worktree is coherent AND the surfaces it just built still match their contracts. architecture_check aggregates 54 of the others. Kept small enough to stay a bootstrap, not a CI run.",
    "ci": "ci.yml's Python job + tools/run_ci_locally.sh. Every contract check, individually, so a failure names the check that found it.",
    "ci-rust": "ci.yml's Rust job (and ./init.sh --full). The same checks re-run with --require-cargo, which turns a missing-cargo SKIP into a FAILURE. Before the registry these ran cargo-strict ONLY inside init.sh on a developer's machine \u2014 CI never enforced the compile smoke."
  },
